# Stage handoff. The verbs leave files here for each other — the request,
# both plans, the commit message, the validation report, the assembled PR
# body. It is scratch, never part of a change: nothing in it may ever be
# committed. This entry is the first line of that defence (a `git add -A`
# cannot pick up an ignored path); the validate verb is the second, and fails
# any commit that touches it anyway, because `git add -f` exists.
.falconet/

# The same directory under its old name, kept while wayfinders-infra is still
# running the stage scripts. handoff_dir is configurable for exactly this.
.ci-handoff/

# Test scratch
/tmp/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Local agent permission rules — MUST stay untracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The Go binary, built out of tree: `go build -o dist/falconet ./cmd/falconet`
/dist/

# python3 byte-code the tests leave behind when they import the fake API
__pycache__/
